The paper makes a real contribution — identifying the FFN bottleneck in prefilling and proposing a simple, training-free, effective solution. The evaluation covers multiple models (7B to 72B) and tasks, with consistently positive results. However, the paper's weaknesses (importance metric validated only against random, missing ablations of N and η, no comparison with joint attention+FFN pruning) are below the threshold expected for a clear accept at ICLR. The paper is comparable to GemFilter and OrthoRank (both 5.25 and rejected) in terms of evaluation depth, despite a somewhat stronger contribution. With the missing ablations addressed, this paper could become a solid accept.

